<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>Evaluating the similarity between simulated and real user messages in math tutoring and document creation tasks across three metrics: <span id="A4.T11.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Writing Style</span> and <span id="A4.T11.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Interaction Style</span> are assessed on a 5-point Likert scale (1=least similar, 5=most similar). <span id="A4.T11.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Turing Test</span> is calculated as <math id="A4.T11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p-50|\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p-50|\%</annotation></semantics></math>, where p is the percentage of correct identification by an LLM evaluator. A value of <math id="A4.T11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\%</annotation></semantics></math> indicates indistinguishability (i.e., random chance).</figcaption>
</figure>
