<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_inline-block" style="width:134.3pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"></span><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.1pt;"> </span><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:113.2pt;">
<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Math Problem: The harmonic mean of two positive integers is the reciprocal of the arithmetic mean of their reciprocals. For how many ordered pairs (x,y) of positive integers is the harmonic mean of x and y equal to 20?</span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p" style="width:134.3pt;"><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_inline-block" style="width:134.3pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:134.3pt;"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p" style="width:134.3pt;"><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_inline-block" style="width:134.3pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"></span><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.1pt;"> </span><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.3.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:113.2pt;">
<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">User Turn 5: Thank you so much for your help! I understand how to find the pairs now and how to factor the equation properly. I feel much more confident with harmonic means and solving these types of problems. Thanks again!</span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p" style="width:134.3pt;"><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_inline-block" style="width:134.3pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:134.3pt;"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p" style="width:134.3pt;"><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_inline-block" style="width:134.3pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"></span><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.1pt;"> </span><span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.2.5.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:113.2pt;">
<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A7.F18.p1.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">AI Tutor Turn 5: You’re very welcome! I’m glad to hear that you feel more confident with harmonic means and solving these types of problems. Remember, practice is key, and you’re doing great! If you have any more questions in the future or need further clarification on any topic, feel free to ask. Happy studying!</span>
</span></span></span></span>
