<span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p" style="width:134.3pt;"><span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_inline-block" style="width:134.3pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"></span><span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.2.2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.1pt;"> </span><span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.2.2.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:113.2pt;">
<span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Math Problem: The harmonic mean of two positive integers is the reciprocal of the arithmetic mean of their reciprocals. For how many ordered pairs (x,y) of positive integers is the harmonic mean of x and y equal to 20?</span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p" style="width:134.3pt;"><span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_inline-block" style="width:134.3pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span id="A7.F22.p2.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:134.3pt;"></span></span></span>
